Artefacts
1. Scholarly article:"Business process improvement opportunities and redesign options: a systematic literature review" (Emerald Publishing, 2025)

Summary of the chosen artefact:
This article performs a systematic literature review based on practical case studies (e.g. a case study of reengineering of a platform of cross docking (PCD) using the Supply Chain Operation Reference Model (SCOR) in a car assembly unit (Aboulaid et al., 2016, p. 1)). Importantly, its findings reveal eighty distinct improvement iopportunities in the business process, and paired with 64 redesign options. Moreover, it presents a structured catalog so that analysyst can utilize in analyzing and improving business processes, which highlights identifying practical problems and corresponding solutions.

The reasons behind choosing this artefact:
I chose this artefact because it directly illustrates modern process analysis techniques, which helps to distinguish different analysis methods (such as reviewing case studies to identify bottlenecks and inefficiencies) from other tools in BPM. It is meaningful because it was published in 2025, which reflects the latest trends in data-driven analysis, and it supports my understanding of how to apply these techniques in practice for process redesign. This demonstrates the development of my knowledge from theory to practical application within organisations.


































